                    },
                    "message": "The changes look good to me. Could you please mention which SoC EVB you are using to test these changes?\nI have ASPEED and Nuvoton EVB setups. I will test on a different SoC than yours so that we can cover multiple SoCs"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "I've tested it on AST2600 EVB. Can you please test it on Nuvoton EVB?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Hariharan Rangasamy",
                        "email": "hariharanr@ami.com",
                        "username": "hariharanrangasamy"
                    },
                    "message": "I don\u2019t need this MR to wait for my testing, as I\u2019ll need some time to validate it on Nuvoton. I should be able to complete testing by early next week.\nDo you want these changes to be merged soon, or can we wait a bit so others can also review and share their feedback?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jae Hyun Yoo",
                        "email": "jae.yoo@oss.qualcomm.com",
                        "username": "jaehyoo"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think there's any need to rush. The most important thing is making sure this change works across all supported BMC SoCs. If it ends up breaking on a particular platform, that's a much bigger problem. It's better to test it thoroughly and merge it once we're confident in the results. That's why I usually let changes sit for about a week before merging them as well."
                },
